  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZIMCODD-Fostering Gender Just Recoveries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant to Christian Aid is for a project to advance gender-just macroeconomic policymaking in the pandemic recovery context in Africa. Ultimately, this project aims to contribute to Christian Aid&#x2019;s long-term economic justice vision in which economies are transformed at the local, national, regional and global levels to serve and be shaped by the voices of marginalized communities. We aim to build new social contracts that fulfil human rights, value care, are sustainable and heal the earth, in ways that are rooted in restorative justice.&#xa0;Through learning, convening and influencing, we aim to do so by addressing the ways in which neoliberal macroeconomic policymaking and undemocratic decision-making structures continue to exacerbate gender inequalities and undermine women&#x2019;s rights, which has become particularly poignant over the last two years in Africa in the context of the Covid-19 pandemic.</narrative>
  </description>
